window.docContents[138].resolve({"/Lists/#Logical-Foundations--Lists___-Working-with-Structured-Data--Pairs-of-Numbers--Structures":{"contents":"Lean also provides a convenient way to define inductive structures like pairs\nthat have a single constructor but multiple ways to access their data,\nusing the structure keyword. The definition of NatProd' below is equivalent\nto the NatProd definition from earlier, except that Lean automatically\ngenerates the fst and snd accessors.\n\n\n\nstructure NatProd' where\n  fst : Nat\n  snd : Nat\n\n#check (NatProd'.mk 3 5)\nexample : (NatProd'.mk 3 5).fst = 3 := by rfl\nexample : (⟨3, 5⟩ : NatProd').fst = 3 := by rfl\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Lists: Working with Structured Data\u0009Pairs of Numbers","header":"5.1.1. Structures","id":"/Lists/#Logical-Foundations--Lists___-Working-with-Structured-Data--Pairs-of-Numbers--Structures"},"/Typeclasses/#Logical-Foundations--Typeclasses--Using-Typeclasses":{"contents":"Let's check what == meant for List.elemNat, with notation display turned off:\n\nset_option pp.notation false in\n#check 1 == 2\n\n\nBEq.beq 1 2 : Bool\n\n\nRather than Nat.beq, == turns out to be notation for BEq.beq, a field of exactly\nthe kind of typeclass we just learned to define:\n\n  class BEq (α : Type) where\n    beq : α → α → Bool\n\n\nWriting x == y makes Lean search for an instance of BEq for the type of x and y, the same\nway it searched for a DefaultValue instance above. For Nat, that instance is:\n\nWhat is (priority := low)? Do the students need to know why that's there?\n\ninstance (priority := low) : BEq Nat where\n  beq := Nat.beq\n\n\nThis is the instance Lean supplies for [BEq α] when List.elemPoly is called on a\nList Nat — no different from Lean choosing instDefaultValueNat for\nDefaultValue.value earlier when it was equated with (1 : Nat).\n\nProve that List.elemPoly agrees with List.elemNat when specialized to\nnatural numbers.theorem List.elemPoly_eq_elemNat (ms : List Nat) (n : Nat) : ms.elemPoly n = ms.elemNat n := by\n  solution!(\n  induction ms with\n  | nil =>\n    rewrite [List.elemPoly_nil, List.elem_nat_nil]\n    rfl\n  | cons hd tl ih =>\n    rewrite [List.elemPoly_cons, List.elem_nat_cons, ih]\n    rfl)\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Typeclasses","header":"11.3. Using Typeclasses","id":"/Typeclasses/#Logical-Foundations--Typeclasses--Using-Typeclasses"}});